WEBVTT

00:15.670 --> 00:18.500
I never dreamed before

00:18.500 --> 00:21.340
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.340 --> 00:24.910
into the world of perfect free

00:24.910 --> 00:27.010
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:27.010 --> 00:29.850
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.850 --> 00:32.580
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.580 --> 00:36.150
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.150 --> 00:37.320
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.320 --> 00:40.230
I was made to hit in America

00:40.230 --> 00:43.090
(I was made to hit in America)

00:43.090 --> 00:49.000
I was made to hit in America

00:49.000 --> 00:52.670
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.670 --> 00:54.670
(To me, forever)

00:54.670 --> 00:58.380
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.380 --> 01:01.610
(To me, forever)

01:08.450 --> 01:14.060
I was made to hit in America

01:14.060 --> 01:16.900
I was made to hit in America

01:16.900 --> 01:19.760
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.760 --> 01:22.570
I was made to hit in America

01:22.570 --> 01:25.340
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.340 --> 01:33.210
I was made to hit in America

01:38.250 --> 01:44.760
Yeah...Yeah...Okay. I'll leave
everything about the contract to you.

01:44.760 --> 01:46.420
Yeah...

01:46.420 --> 01:50.100
What? The band name
"Beck" is no good there?

01:50.100 --> 01:54.100
Then you name something
works good in U.S.

01:54.100 --> 01:57.270
Yeah. I'll send you the DAT
as soon as possible.

01:57.270 --> 01:59.100
Okay. 'Bye...

02:02.440 --> 02:05.840
Hey, Ryusuke! Are you here?

02:09.450 --> 02:12.620
What?! An overseas debut?

02:12.620 --> 02:16.620
So easily? I mean...we're lucky.

02:16.620 --> 02:19.460
No, I don't think
we should expect too much.

02:19.460 --> 02:23.630
True, it's the U.S.,
but this is a very obscure label.

02:23.630 --> 02:29.800
Yeah...Um...Mr. Albin...
The guy with the name card, right?

02:29.800 --> 02:33.310
But, I can feel the enthusiasm in him.

02:33.310 --> 02:38.240
He says Beck is the best band
he's heard in Japan.

02:38.240 --> 02:39.680
Hmm...

02:42.150 --> 02:45.080
America! Blonde beauties.

02:54.430 --> 02:57.420
I wonder if we'd fit in better overseas...

02:59.100 --> 03:01.090
America?

03:13.040 --> 03:18.000
"Live 17
'Three Days'"

03:18.970 --> 03:21.400
Here you go.

03:21.400 --> 03:23.300
Thank you very much!

03:30.480 --> 03:33.150
Unusual for a customer be so thankful...

03:33.150 --> 03:38.850
Yeah...I haven't seen a customer
so happy in a long time.

04:04.780 --> 04:07.450
Yukio! You're too loud!

04:07.450 --> 04:09.450
Oh...I'm sorry!

04:09.450 --> 04:13.850
Let's see...Volume...volume...Okay.

04:35.480 --> 04:37.740
Oh? Till morning?

04:37.740 --> 04:44.420
Yeah. It's completely different
from a Gretsch so it's a lot of fun!

04:44.420 --> 04:45.750
A Telecaster?

04:45.750 --> 04:49.260
Mm-hmm...I even took
a day off my job for this.

04:49.260 --> 04:50.760
I see...

04:50.760 --> 04:54.190
-Be careful you don't lose your job!
-Uh-huh...

05:20.790 --> 05:22.550
Oh! That girl!

05:31.130 --> 05:33.790
-Oh...It is!
-Huh?!

05:39.910 --> 05:43.540
Ooh...Ouch...

05:45.580 --> 05:46.750
Are you all right?

05:46.750 --> 05:49.250
I-I guess so...

05:49.250 --> 05:54.420
You...Aren't you the girl
working at the donut shop?

05:54.420 --> 05:56.910
Tanaka...kun?

06:00.830 --> 06:02.600
"Health Room"

06:02.600 --> 06:03.230
"Health Room"

06:02.600 --> 06:03.230
How did you know my name?

06:03.230 --> 06:05.270
How did you know my name?

06:05.270 --> 06:07.930
Well, you're always getting scolded.

06:07.930 --> 06:10.990
Oh, is that why? How embarrassing!

06:12.940 --> 06:14.940
Okay. I'm done.

06:14.940 --> 06:18.110
It's nothing serious, but be
careful for two or three days.

06:18.110 --> 06:19.510
All right.

06:21.450 --> 06:24.620
The employees aren't treated
very well at that shop.

06:24.620 --> 06:28.790
That's why the worker
turnover is so great.

06:28.790 --> 06:32.130
Tanaka-kun...Can you play the guitar?

06:32.130 --> 06:34.130
Huh? You can play, can't you?

06:34.130 --> 06:36.290
No. Not at all.

06:37.730 --> 06:40.570
I...This guitar case...

06:40.570 --> 06:42.760
I saw it in the Light Music Club room.

06:43.900 --> 06:47.430
Yeah...The club leader yelled at me,
so I quit after three days.

06:48.910 --> 06:50.910
Your name?

06:50.910 --> 06:54.070
Oh! I'm Hiromi Masuoka.

06:55.250 --> 07:09.400
Hiromi Masuoka...Hiromi Masuoka...
Hiromi Masuoka...

07:09.400 --> 07:15.230
Hiromi Masuoka, Hiromi Masuoka...

07:28.450 --> 07:32.180
Hiromi Masuoka...

07:33.790 --> 07:35.960
Wow...

07:35.960 --> 07:39.390
Why, you're good, Tanaka-kun.

07:39.390 --> 07:43.230
What's that song you just sang?

07:43.230 --> 07:46.230
It's a song called Face by Beck.

07:46.230 --> 07:48.740
I'm impressed, Tanaka-kun.

07:48.740 --> 07:53.760
Thank you. This guitar seems to be fine.

07:56.910 --> 08:00.740
-Shall I give you lessons, then?
-Yes. Thank you!

08:09.420 --> 08:13.260
Thank you for letting me use
your White Falcon all this time.

08:14.260 --> 08:17.260
Mm-hmm...Let me know anytime
you want to use it.

08:17.260 --> 08:18.930
You can borrow it anytime.

08:18.930 --> 08:20.090
All right.

08:29.940 --> 08:33.280
Uh...hello...I'm ready anytime.

08:33.280 --> 08:35.780
What about you, Momo-chan?

08:35.780 --> 08:39.650
I see. Then, see you as usual
in front of the dog...Bye...

08:41.890 --> 08:43.380
Momoko-sensei!

08:47.060 --> 08:51.230
Actually, word got out that I once
worked for a week at a cabaret club

08:51.230 --> 08:54.070
thanks to a former student.

08:54.070 --> 08:57.900
It became a problem among the staff
when they found out I had kept it a secret.

08:57.900 --> 09:00.570
It was such a shock.
I was really troubled over it.

09:00.570 --> 09:03.410
I tried going to various seminars...

09:03.410 --> 09:06.910
-And then...
-I became her confidant.

09:06.910 --> 09:09.920
No one understands better than I do
about the entertainment business.

09:09.920 --> 09:12.420
Yeah, better than anyone...

09:12.420 --> 09:14.750
Ouch!

09:14.750 --> 09:20.590
Our relationship is still platonic,
so don't go saying anything unnecessary.

09:20.590 --> 09:22.760
Mm...

09:22.760 --> 09:26.100
So long, Koyuki-kun!

09:26.100 --> 09:31.590
Kenichi Saito, 44...Currently dashing
through the roads of his youth.

09:37.880 --> 09:42.720
I haven't seen you
at work recently, Masuoka-san.

09:42.720 --> 09:46.690
The truth is, I made a mistake
that was a big blow to the shop,

09:46.690 --> 09:49.720
and so they fired me...

09:49.720 --> 09:53.730
But I'm really excited
about the new club I joined!

09:53.730 --> 09:55.900
Oh...

09:55.900 --> 09:57.190
So long...

10:02.740 --> 10:05.570
Grade 10-B, Hiromi Masuoka...

10:05.570 --> 10:07.300
Huh? You know her?

10:08.570 --> 10:10.600
Sure. I've checked her out.

10:20.250 --> 10:22.420
Ohh...

10:22.420 --> 10:26.260
When she was in intermediate school,
she had a good record.

10:26.260 --> 10:27.760
Oh?

10:27.760 --> 10:31.430
I wonder if she wouldn't
come to our live show...

10:31.430 --> 10:32.920
I wonder...

10:34.430 --> 10:39.140
Hiromi, why don't you take
a break? You must be thirsty.

10:39.140 --> 10:41.210
-Here.
-Thanks!

10:41.210 --> 10:43.480
Okay! I'll invite her later.

10:43.480 --> 10:44.370
Huh?

11:03.630 --> 11:07.220
"Belle Ame-First National Live House Tour"
"Expectations High for New Band"

11:09.570 --> 11:11.230
Beck...eat it.

11:24.750 --> 11:28.780
Hello? Hey, Mr. Albin...
Hey, how's our CD going?

11:31.920 --> 11:33.080
What?!

12:35.990 --> 12:42.600
Brother...It's because of your victory...
that I am now able to walk!

12:42.600 --> 12:46.100
Huh...Don't be silly...

12:46.100 --> 12:49.830
Brother...Brother!!

13:21.130 --> 13:23.970
Thank you very much!

13:23.970 --> 13:25.160
Hmm...

13:29.310 --> 13:31.640
What are you doing, kid?!

13:31.640 --> 13:33.110
I'm sorry!

13:36.580 --> 13:37.920
...feel totally loose

13:37.920 --> 13:39.250
This crazy, crazy world

13:39.250 --> 13:42.020
You just have to Stage Dive or Die

13:42.020 --> 13:43.920
Mind blower, a shower of sweat

13:43.920 --> 13:46.260
Run towards a new world, my life

13:46.260 --> 13:48.860
Those who seek it will be rewarded

13:48.860 --> 13:50.100
Pass the hot shot

13:50.100 --> 13:52.270
Keep on coming, come on!

13:52.270 --> 13:53.770
Blow your mind

13:53.770 --> 13:55.700
What are you doing, Koyuki?!

14:05.110 --> 14:06.950
Boy, am I hungry.

14:06.950 --> 14:08.450
Yeah...

14:08.450 --> 14:10.450
Let's have some ramen noodles
before we head home.

14:10.450 --> 14:12.290
Hmm...Good idea.

14:12.290 --> 14:13.680
Ramen again?!

14:26.130 --> 14:27.970
Yo!

14:27.970 --> 14:28.970
Huh?

14:28.970 --> 14:31.300
Sorry to keep you waiting.

14:31.300 --> 14:33.640
Where's Ryusuke-kun?

14:33.640 --> 14:36.670
Something came up so he gave me
the tickets and told me to go.

14:38.510 --> 14:41.500
"'Three Days' Directed by Jim Walsh-
No.1 hit in U.S.!!"

14:46.590 --> 14:48.420
Why are you always like this?!

14:48.420 --> 14:52.760
What can I do? Our way
of living is too different.

14:52.760 --> 14:55.930
Right. That's it, then.

14:55.930 --> 14:57.760
Maybe...

14:57.760 --> 14:59.930
I still love you.

14:59.930 --> 15:02.440
Me, too.

15:02.440 --> 15:03.490
Take care.

15:09.940 --> 15:13.450
-The movie was a little hard to understand,
but the characters were so real

15:09.940 --> 15:13.450
-It's been a while. How's life?

15:13.450 --> 15:15.280
-The movie was a little hard to understand,
but the characters were so real

15:13.450 --> 15:15.280
-I'm alive...

15:15.280 --> 15:18.120
-that when the movie ended,
I felt a little sad leaving them.

15:15.280 --> 15:18.120
-It's a tough world.

15:18.120 --> 15:20.850
-That when the movie ended,
I felt a little sad leaving them.

15:18.120 --> 15:20.850
-Yeah.

15:22.960 --> 15:28.130
Jim Walsh...This director is a genius!

15:28.130 --> 15:29.960
Yeah. It was interesting.

15:29.960 --> 15:31.990
Why, I didn't get sleepy at all.

15:33.630 --> 15:37.240
I hear this movie is such a hit that
Dying Breed's concert tour movie

15:37.240 --> 15:40.240
is going to be released
simultaneously in the U.S. And Japan.

15:40.240 --> 15:42.640
Oh? Their concert tour movie?

16:01.260 --> 16:03.100
Hi!

16:03.100 --> 16:07.770
Maho, I'm going to have dinner with Morita
and Eguchi-san, whom I'm playing with.

16:07.770 --> 16:09.770
Are you free on Saturday?

16:09.770 --> 16:14.770
That's nice, but I've got a Beck's live.

16:14.770 --> 16:17.280
He says he's having
dinner with Eguchi-san!

16:17.280 --> 16:18.610
Huh?!

16:18.610 --> 16:20.780
Huh?!

16:20.780 --> 16:22.620
Call me again the next time.

16:22.620 --> 16:24.710
-What?! You're not gonna say you...
-Bye!

16:27.620 --> 16:29.960
Now...Let's go and get something to eat.

16:29.960 --> 16:31.120
Okay!

16:38.260 --> 16:40.570
What? Really!

16:40.570 --> 16:43.900
Yeah. They seem to be selling pretty well.

16:43.900 --> 16:45.530
Our song...

16:48.410 --> 16:51.410
Seems it's unusual for a Japanese band.

16:51.410 --> 16:53.250
That president gets things done.

16:53.250 --> 16:56.750
Uh...His name was Albin-san, was it?

16:56.750 --> 16:57.880
What's wrong?

16:59.250 --> 17:00.420
What's wrong?

17:00.420 --> 17:03.390
I should've signed
the contract for royalties.

17:07.090 --> 17:09.930
What? You mean it doesn't matter
how many copies they sell?!

17:09.930 --> 17:11.930
-So no matter how many
copies they sell...
-Ouch!

17:11.930 --> 17:14.460
What...What? Aargh!

17:24.780 --> 17:26.610
Spice!

17:28.110 --> 17:30.140
Check, check, check, check...

17:33.620 --> 17:35.120
Uh! Uh!

17:35.120 --> 17:37.560
Blow your mind

17:37.560 --> 17:40.060
Squeeze your sweat yeah

17:40.060 --> 17:42.390
Blow your mind

17:42.390 --> 17:44.730
Squeeze your sweat yeah

17:44.730 --> 17:47.230
Blow your mind

17:47.230 --> 17:49.570
Squeeze your sweat yeah

17:49.570 --> 17:52.170
Blow your mind

17:52.170 --> 17:53.330
Squeeze your sweat

18:03.080 --> 18:07.250
Large lips in the motion

18:07.250 --> 18:11.590
Trying to keep blaming on

18:11.590 --> 18:16.100
As I say reason I'm late on

18:16.100 --> 18:18.260
Find you turning

18:18.260 --> 18:20.930
Laughing and smiling

18:35.950 --> 18:39.220
My ears are still ringing...
but it was really great.

18:39.220 --> 18:41.590
Really? I'm glad.

18:41.590 --> 18:42.560
Right, Saku?

18:42.560 --> 18:44.060
Yeah, for real.

18:44.060 --> 18:46.560
It was awesome!

18:46.560 --> 18:49.900
And the crowd was huge!

18:49.900 --> 18:53.570
Little by little we've been
getting bigger crowds.

18:53.570 --> 18:55.400
Come again, Masuoka-san.

18:55.400 --> 18:57.370
-I will!
-Hmph!

19:00.570 --> 19:03.240
I hear Beck's playing
at the Marquee next.

19:03.240 --> 19:05.080
No way...That's terrific!

19:05.080 --> 19:07.200
They're really gaining in popularity.

19:08.410 --> 19:11.250
Say, didn't that guy look
like Yoshito Morozumi?

19:11.250 --> 19:13.420
No way...Really?

19:13.420 --> 19:15.350
He wouldn't be in a place like this...

19:16.760 --> 19:20.890
Hmph! They're nothing but
a little-known amateur band!

19:29.770 --> 19:32.610
There was a message from the president.

19:32.610 --> 19:35.440
They're going to print
more copies of our CD.

19:47.990 --> 19:51.390
So our music is playing in America?

19:51.390 --> 19:52.450
Yeah...

19:53.730 --> 19:55.560
-Say...
-Huh?

19:55.560 --> 19:57.530
Can you tell me the story?

20:01.570 --> 20:03.540
Where did you get it?

20:06.910 --> 20:08.370
I stole it.

20:13.250 --> 20:14.640
You broke into cars?!

20:21.250 --> 20:24.920
We had time on our hands,
so Eddy and I often did it.

20:24.920 --> 20:27.950
And then we came upon that hot car.

20:31.760 --> 20:33.700
What surprised us more was...

20:36.100 --> 20:37.870
That's Lucille!

20:37.870 --> 20:41.210
What? This car is no good, Eddy.

20:41.210 --> 20:43.880
No, look! This is Sonny Boy Waters' guitar.

20:43.880 --> 20:47.050
He's a blues guitarist.
Even Eric Clapton respects him.

20:47.050 --> 20:48.880
He's a legend.

20:48.880 --> 20:50.220
Sonny Boy?

20:50.220 --> 20:53.890
Serial Number...8-3001...

20:53.890 --> 20:55.150
Dude, that's it!

20:55.150 --> 20:56.890
Come on! Let's go!

20:56.890 --> 20:58.560
See, Sonny Boy and this guy were

20:58.560 --> 21:01.390
fighting over this woman
called Lucille in a night club.

21:01.390 --> 21:04.400
And the guy shot Sonny Boy
right on the stage.

21:04.400 --> 21:05.900
You mean, during the play?

21:05.900 --> 21:09.970
The guitar's been called Lucille
ever since then.

21:09.970 --> 21:11.560
That's insane...

21:13.570 --> 21:16.340
Okay. Let's get outta here. Come on.

21:18.240 --> 21:19.800
Hey, Ray!

21:21.910 --> 21:24.080
I kind of like this guitar.

21:24.080 --> 21:24.910
What?

21:26.750 --> 21:29.350
I'll be the legend after Sonny Boy.

21:33.760 --> 21:34.990
-Huh?
-Huh?

21:36.760 --> 21:39.290
And that's when I met up with Beck.

21:48.770 --> 21:50.780
I found out later...

21:50.780 --> 21:53.610
The car belonged to
someone really dangerous.

21:53.610 --> 21:58.110
And now he's searching frantically
for Beck and Lucille.

22:12.660 --> 22:16.120
"Director Jim Walsh's Newest Film-
Dying Breed's Road Tour Movie"

22:30.480 --> 22:34.820
Hey! We have a group in. Your break is up.

22:34.820 --> 22:36.880
Okay...I'll be right there!

22:50.370 --> 22:52.470
Another minute

22:52.470 --> 22:55.170
Feelin' so fine

22:57.480 --> 22:59.710
You turn the freeze

22:59.710 --> 23:02.440
into warm light

23:04.550 --> 23:08.020
Had a premonition

23:08.020 --> 23:10.690
I've been waitin' ever since

23:10.690 --> 23:14.190
My world comin' down

23:14.190 --> 23:16.990
It's got me spinnin' 'round

23:18.760 --> 23:24.940
If you really wanna fly

23:24.940 --> 23:27.700
you gotta let go

23:39.950 --> 23:42.290
Simply the most

23:42.290 --> 23:44.320
big sensation

23:44.320 --> 23:47.130
(once you're here you won't go back)

23:47.130 --> 23:49.390
She's really pretty

23:49.390 --> 23:51.400
One-eyed vision

23:51.400 --> 23:54.230
(lose the fear it don't come back)

23:54.230 --> 23:57.740
Little sister showed me

23:57.740 --> 24:00.410
Really took me for a ride

24:00.410 --> 24:02.070
My world comin' down

24:02.070 --> 24:05.410
(once you're here you won't go back)

24:05.410 --> 24:09.440
(lose the fear it don't come back)

24:13.550 --> 24:14.890
-I'm Atsushi.
-I'm Eriko.

24:14.890 --> 24:16.220
-Together we are...
-The Chipped Teapot...Boing...

24:16.220 --> 24:17.390
"Live 18 'Leon Sykes'"

24:16.220 --> 24:17.390
-Together we are...
-The Chipped Teapot...Boing...

24:17.390 --> 24:18.890
"Live 18 'Leon Sykes'"

24:17.390 --> 24:18.890
Bonny Jump is doing a live show.

24:18.890 --> 24:20.150
"Live 18 'Leon Sykes'"

24:18.890 --> 24:20.150
-Be sure to come...
...and watch.
